            "role": "DIRECTOR, HUMAN AI LAB",
            "title": "DIRECTOR, HUMAN AI LAB",
            "bio": "Eng. Prof. Indika Perera is a Professor in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at the University of Moratuwa, Sri Lanka, and serves as the Director of the HumanAI Research Lab, an interdisciplinary initiative focused on advancing human-centered artificial intelligence through research and innovation. He holds a PhD in Computer Science from the University of St Andrews, United Kingdom, along with an MSc from the University of Moratuwa and an MBS and PGDBM from the University of Colombo, Sri Lanka. His research contributions span software engineering, software architecture and quality, technology-enhanced learning, immersive technologies, human-computer interaction, and emerging computing paradigms. Prof. Indika has contributed to numerous research publications and collaborative initiatives, exploring the intersection of software systems, intelligent technologies, and human-centered design. Through HumanAI Research Lab, he leads efforts toward developing responsible, innovative, and impactful AI solutions while fostering interdisciplinary collaboration and nurturing future researchers in artificial intelligence and related fields.",
